'''Factions''' are a feature exclusive to the [[Crimson Isle]]. There are currently two factions: Mages and Barbarians, whom are enemies with each other. By allying themselves with one of the factions, the player can access the faction's [[Community Center]] to do tasks for them, interact with the Faction's shops, and gain reputation with them. Players can swap factions at any time. 

One can see a player's faction by looking at their icon besides their name in the Tab menu.

== How to join a Faction ==
{{Main|Crimson Isle Main Questline}}
In order to join a faction, the player must partially complete the main questline by talking to {{NPCSprite|Elle}}. 

== Factions ==
=== {{Faction|Mage}} ===
The Mage faction is one of the two factions on the [[Crimson Isle]]. It is located on the right side of the island and is led by {{NPCSprite|Queen Nyx}}. The Mage faction has its own [[Bank]], [[Auction House]], and [[Bazaar]], as well as its local [[Blacksmith]], {{NPCSprite|Alwin}}, and {{Zone|Scarleton}} is patrolled by guards. <!--[[File:Mage Guard.png|thumb|64px]]-->

=== {{Faction|Barbarian}} ===
The Barbarian faction is one of the two factions on the [[Crimson Isle]]. It is located on the left side of the island and is led by {{NPCSprite|Chief Scorn}}. The Barbarian faction has its own [[Bank]], [[Auction House]], and [[Bazaar]], as well as its local [[Blacksmith]], {{NPCSprite|Igor}}, and {{Zone|Dragontail}} is patrolled by guards. <!--[[File:Barbarian Guard.png|thumb|64px]]-->

== Reputation ==
Reputation is a mechanic in which the player can get friendlier with their current '''Faction''', allowing them to unlock new items, trades from NPCs, and much more.

The player will have {{red|0}} reputation with both factions at the start. Advancing through their '''Faction's''' questline will earn them reputation. Other ways to earn reputation include completing Daily missions at the Community Center, and short quests given by '''Faction''' [[NPC]]s.

If one kills {{NPCSprite|Fire Mage;Fire Mages}} or {{NPCSprite|Barbarian;Barbarians}}, their reputation for the respective faction is reduced by {{Red|5}}.

=== Titles ===
The player's title changes when they reach certain {{Reputation}} milestones.
*Neutral: {{Reputation||0}}
*Friendly: {{Reputation||1,000}}
*Trusted: {{Reputation||3,000}}
*Honored: {{Reputation||7,000}}
*Hero: {{Reputation||12,000}}

Additionally, the player receives {{SkyBlock XP}} for achieving certain titles in each faction:
*Friendly: {{SkyBlock XP|5}}
*Trusted: {{SkyBlock XP|10}}
*Honored: {{SkyBlock XP|20}}
*Hero: {{SkyBlock XP|40}}

=== Earning {{Reputation|mage}} ===
There are several ways to earn {{Reputation|mage}}. These include:
*Completing the {{Faction|Mage}} questline: {{Green|+600}}
** Presenting the stolen research: {{Green|+100}}
** Giving {{NPCSprite|Dean}} the {{Item|Magma Chunk}}s and {{Item|Burning Eye}}s: {{Green|+150}}
** Helping {{NPCSprite|Igrupan}}: {{Green|+50}}
** Helping {{NPCSprite|Odexar}}: {{Green|+100}} (and {{Coins|80}})
** Defeating [[Kuudra]]: {{Green|+200}}
*Completing [[Faction Quests]]: {{Green|+30-125}}
*7 days of daily fights against {{NPCSprite|Rollim}}: {{Green|+25}} (Per day)
*Giving {{NPCSprite|Pablo}} the flower they ask for: {{Green|+25}} (Every 2 days)
*Giving {{NPCSprite|Avorius}} a {{Item|Cup of Blood}}: {{Green|+5}} (Every 3 days)
*Throwing a {{Item|Titanic Experience Bottle}} on {{NPCSprite|Mollim}}: {{Green|+20}} (Only once)
*Killing mini-bosses daily: {{Green|+20}} per mini-boss
*Killing [[Kuudra]] daily: {{Green|+10/20/30/40/50}} for killing basic/hot/burning/fiery/infernal Kuudra tier (Per day)
*Killing {{NPCSprite|Barbarian;Barbarians}}: {{Green|+25}} (Only with negative {{Reputation|mage}})
*Completing the {{NPCSprite|Alchemage}}'s quest: {{Green|+250}} (Only once)
*Killing {{NPCSprite|Chickzilla}}: {{Green|+100}} available at 7000 mage reputation (Only once)

=== Earning {{Reputation|Barbarian}} ===
There are several ways to earn {{Reputation|Barbarian}}. These include:
*Completing the {{Faction|Barbarian}} questline: {{Green|+900}} / {{Green|920}} ({{Green|+20}} from the [[Magma Boss]])
** Presenting the stolen research: {{Green|+100}}
** Completing {{NPCSprite|Ugo}}'s training and defeating the {{NPCSprite|Magma Boss}}: {{Green|+150}} / {{Green|+170}} ({{Green|+20}} from the [[Magma Boss]])
** Helping out {{NPCSprite|Lasea}}: {{Green|+100}}
** Helping out {{NPCSprite|Gris}}: {{Green|+150}} (and {{Coins|200,000}})
** Defeating [[Kuudra]]: {{Green|+200}}
** Speaking to {{NPCSprite|Chief Scorn}} after defeating [[Kuudra]]: {{Green|+200}}
*Completing [[Faction Quests]]: {{Green|+30-125}}
*7 days of daily fights against {{NPCSprite|Kaus}}: {{Green|+25}} (Per day)
*Killing mini-bosses daily: {{Green|+20}} per mini-boss
*Killing [[Kuudra]] daily: {{Green|+10/20/30/40/50}} for killing basic/hot/burning/fiery/infernal Kuudra tier (Per day)
*Completing {{NPCSprite|Baar}}'s quest: {{Green|+250}} (Only once)
*Giving {{NPCSprite|Pomtair}} {{Item|Enchanted Bone Meal}}: {{Green|+50}} (Per day)
*Killing {{NPCSprite|Fire Mage;Fire Mages}}: {{Green|+25}} (Only with negative {{Reputation|barbarian}})
*Giving {{NPCSprite|Sirih}} {{Item|Sulphur}}: {{Green|+10}} (Every 2 days)
*Finding {{NPCSprite|Turd}}'s toy and giving it back to {{NPCSprite|Suus}}: {{Green|+40}} (Every 5 days)

== Trivia ==
*The [[Minions|Minion]] merchants of both factions don't require reputation to access. Only the {{Item|Mycelium Minion}} and {{Item|Red Sand Minion}} require reputation to purchase.
*According to text that appears when visiting {{Zone|Scarleton}} for the first time, members of the Mage Faction are known as Taika.

